{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 27,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not boast about tomorrow, for you do not know what a day may bring.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let another praise you, and not your own mouth— a stranger, and not your own lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A stone is heavy and sand is a burden, but aggravation from a fool outweighs them both.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wrath is cruel and anger is like a flood, but who can withstand jealousy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better an open rebuke than love that is concealed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wounds of a friend are faithful, but the kisses of an enemy are deceitful.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The soul that is full loathes honey, but to a hungry soul, any bitter thing is sweet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a bird that strays from its nest is a man who wanders from his home.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oil and incense bring joy to the heart, and the counsel of a friend is sweetness to the soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not forsake your friend or your father’s friend, and do not go to your brother’s house in the day of your calamity; better a neighbor nearby than a brother far away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be wise, my son, and bring joy to my heart, so that I can answer him who taunts me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The prudent see danger and take cover, but the simple keep going and pay the penalty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take the garment of him who posts security for a stranger; get collateral if it is for a foreigner.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If one blesses his neighbor with a loud voice early in the morning, it will be counted to him as a curse.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A constant dripping on a rainy day and a contentious woman are alike —",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "restraining her is like holding back the wind or grasping oil with one’s right hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As iron sharpens iron, so one man sharpens another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever tends a fig tree will eat its fruit, and he who looks after his master will be honored.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As water reflects the face, so the heart reflects the true man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied; so the eyes of man are never satisfied.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A crucible for silver and a furnace for gold, but a man is tested by the praise accorded him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though you grind a fool like grain with mortar and a pestle, yet his folly will not depart from him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be sure to know the state of your flocks, and pay close attention to your herds;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for riches are not forever, nor does a crown endure to every generation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When hay is removed and new growth appears and the grass from the hills is gathered,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "the lambs will provide you with clothing, and the goats with the price of a field.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.27.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You will have plenty of goats’ milk to feed you— food for your household and nourishment for your maidservants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
